## Summary
Fixes #76233.

Approved exec follow-up turns for run-mode subagents can now keep an already materialized bundle MCP runtime alive until their active lease is released. Runtime retirement still starts immediately, blocks new leases, and global shutdown can still force disposal.

## Root cause
`src/agents/agent-bundle-mcp-runtime.ts:1038` disposed a session runtime immediately even when `materializeBundleMcpToolsForRun` already held an active lease:

```before
async dispose() {
  if (disposed) {
    return;
  }
  disposed = true;
  catalog = null;
  catalogInFlight = undefined;
  const sessionsToClose = Array.from(sessions.values());
  sessions.clear();
  await Promise.allSettled(sessionsToClose.map((session) => disposeSession(session)));
}
```

That let subagent cleanup retire the bundle MCP runtime while a late approved follow-up turn was between runtime lookup and tool materialization, producing `bundle-mcp runtime disposed for session ...`.

## Fix
`src/agents/agent-bundle-mcp-runtime.ts:580` now tracks retirement start, waits for active leases before normal disposal, and rejects new leases once retirement begins:

```after
acquireLease() {
  failIfDisposing();
  activeLeases += 1;
  let released = false;
  return () => {
    if (released) {
      return;
    }
    released = true;
    activeLeases = Math.max(0, activeLeases - 1);
    resolveLeaseDrainers();
  };
}
```

`dispose({ force: true })` remains available for `disposeAll()` so process shutdown does not wait on live run leases.

## Why this is the right boundary
The race is at the session MCP runtime ownership boundary, not in the exec follow-up text path. Materialized bundle MCP tools already acquire and release runtime leases; this change makes runtime retirement honor that existing ownership contract. The idle sweeper already skips active leases, and global teardown keeps forceful behavior through the explicit force option.

## Verification
- `PATH=/opt/node/bin:$PATH node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/agents/agent-bundle-mcp-runtime.test.ts src/agents/agent-bundle-mcp-tools.materialize.test.ts` passed 2 Vitest shards in 42.82s. `agent-bundle-mcp-tools.materialize.test.ts`: 13 passed. `agent-bundle-mcp-runtime.test.ts`: 42 passed.
- `PATH=/opt/node/bin:$PATH node scripts/run-oxlint.mjs src/agents/agent-bundle-mcp-runtime.ts src/agents/agent-bundle-mcp-runtime.test.ts src/agents/agent-bundle-mcp-types.ts` passed.
- `PATH=/opt/node/bin:$PATH ./node_modules/.bin/oxfmt --check src/agents/agent-bundle-mcp-runtime.ts src/agents/agent-bundle-mcp-runtime.test.ts src/agents/agent-bundle-mcp-types.ts` passed.
- `PATH=/opt/node/bin:$PATH node scripts/run-tsgo.mjs -p tsconfig.core.json --incremental --tsBuildInfoFile .artifacts/tsgo-cache/core.tsbuildinfo` passed.
- `PATH=/opt/node/bin:$PATH node scripts/run-tsgo.mjs -p test/tsconfig/tsconfig.core.test.json --incremental --tsBuildInfoFile .artifacts/tsgo-cache/core-test.tsbuildinfo` passed.
- Before/after runtime proof used `PATH=/opt/node/bin:$PATH node --import tsx /tmp/openclaw-76233-runtime-proof.ts` against pristine main and this patch with identical input.

## Real behavior proof
Behavior addressed: A session bundle MCP runtime must not retire while an approved follow-up turn still holds an active materialization lease.
Real environment tested: The real source runtime functions `getOrCreateSessionMcpRuntime`, `materializeBundleMcpToolsForRun`, and `retireSessionMcpRuntime` were driven on pristine main fa84741f93b9610c1dbb3e187955cace28a02e44 and on this patched tree e35e7ff0af48dd97cd41ead0441e098300159510; no external network service was involved.
Exact steps or command run after this patch: `PATH=/opt/node/bin:$PATH node --import tsx /tmp/openclaw-76233-runtime-proof.ts`
Evidence after fix:
```
# BEFORE (pristine main fa84741f93b9610c1dbb3e187955cace28a02e44)
{
  "beforeRelease": {
    "activeLeases": 1,
    "retireSettled": true,
    "extraLeaseResult": "accepted"
  },
  "afterRelease": {
    "retireResult": true,
    "retireSettled": true,
    "cachedSessionIds": [],
    "materializeAfterRetire": "rejected: bundle-mcp runtime disposed for session session-proof-76233"
  }
}
# AFTER (this patch e35e7ff0af48dd97cd41ead0441e098300159510, identical input)
{
  "beforeRelease": {
    "activeLeases": 1,
    "retireSettled": false,
    "extraLeaseResult": "rejected: bundle-mcp runtime disposed for session session-proof-76233"
  },
  "afterRelease": {
    "retireResult": true,
    "retireSettled": true,
    "cachedSessionIds": [],
    "materializeAfterRetire": "rejected: bundle-mcp runtime disposed for session session-proof-76233"
  }
}
```
Observed result after fix: Retirement remains pending while one lease is active, new leases are refused during retirement, and final removal happens only after the held lease is released.
What was not tested: No live provider request or real chat UI approval click; full production build was not run because this change is confined to the session bundle MCP runtime lifecycle.
